# .muster/config — project-local sprint-driver knobs (bash-sourced by muster-sprint-run.sh).
# Committed on purpose: worktrees inherit it, so autonomous runs see your settings.
# Precedence: explicit env at invocation > this file > built-in default.
# Uncomment a line to set it. The Guide (/muster) can tune these for you conversationally.

# Run budget — steps per driver run (cost circuit-breaker). Pro-plan suggestion: 8.
#MAX_STEPS=30

# Per-step model-turn budget. Raise for heavy-but-cohesive steps.
#MAX_TURNS=150

# Session-default model for autonomous steps. Per-step `Model:` queue lines still win.
# Pro-plan suggestion: a cheaper model for routine steps, e.g. claude-sonnet-4-6.
#ANTHROPIC_MODEL=

# How many runs of sprint logs to keep in .muster-sprint-logs/.
#KEEP_RUNS=20

# Fallback resume time (HH:MM) when a usage-limit reset time can't be parsed from the error.
#LIMIT_RESUME_AT=
